format session-log-v1
stamp 20260814.121500
editor Zed
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host Ubuntu cloud pier (Eastern EDT convention)
title ALES9 — Lotus's mute and solo, the channel strip's two switches
prompt Continue the autonomous recur (baton prin recur): next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61, STOP only at custody gates.
think Fifth increment of this recur, right after ALES8 (fader column) landed and pushed to both remotes. No custody gate in reach — the Lotus ladder is pure local software.
think Lindy-first crux-first: of ALES8's named next roads (pan · mute/solo · transport loop · crossfade curve), mute and solo are the most durable — the channel strip's two most-used controls after the fader, and they compose DIRECTLY on the fader I just built. Pan waits on stereo (a larger architectural opening); a loop only extends the ALES7 read head; a curve refines the ALES4 fade.
think The one crux: mute/solo add NO new sum and NO new saturation. A Strip resolves to an EFFECTIVE fader (its own fader if audible, else 0/1 silence), then the mix is ALES8's fader.render delegated whole. The only sum in the suite stays the one wide-i64-accumulate-then-saturate-once. The desk rule stated positively: solo, when any track holds it, wins (solo-in-place overrides even a track's own mute); otherwise every un-muted track is heard.
think Designed lotus/strip.rye: Strip{fader,muted,soloed}, any_solo, audible(strip, solo_active) as a positive predicate, resolve → effective fader column, render(session, strips, clock, out) delegating to fader.render. A default column reproduces ALES8 byte-for-byte (channel strip generalizes fader column). ALES8's fader.rye untouched — composed over its public API.
obs GREEN on first build across seven blocks. tame_style_check bans clean (strip.rye carries ≥2 asserts per fn), width-check exit 0, ALES8 fader witness re-run GREEN (strictly additive). render's error union (TrackError || clock.ClockError || timeline.EditError) coerces the delegated try cleanly.
obs Honest scope kept explicit: mute/solo are a pure map from switches to levels, no electrical or hardware claim; purely local, no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device. No custody gate reached.
loom witness=ales_strip_witness cases=7 build=first_green tame=clean width=exit0 ales8_regreen=1
file lotus/strip.rye ALES9 module — Strip/any_solo/audible/resolve/render, mute+solo resolved to an effective fader, mix delegated to ALES8
file tools/ales_strip_witness.rish witness — 7 cases (rest==ALES8, mute, solo, two-solo, solo-over-mute, BadGain, ClipFull), GREEN on metal
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales9-lotus-mute-solo.md self-approved design round for ALES9
file lotus/README.md seated ALES9 in status, rungs, prove-list, road-on
recommend keep-going ALES10 — pan (a fader per channel as stereo opens), a transport loop over a marked region, or the equal-power crossfade curve. No custody gate in reach.
